      "writtenOn": "2023-02-22T17:11:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To clarify things, the config value `CONFIG_BODY_DETECTION_NOTIFY_MODE_CHANGE` hasn\u0027t changed. It\u0027s always had that name since it was added by https://crrev.com/c/3868880.\n\nThe host event that\u0027s sent is being changed from `EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE` to `EC_HOST_EVENT_BODY_DETECT_CHANGE`, to fix the spurious wake bug (b/261141172).\n\n* `EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE`: This is sent when tablet mode changes (enabled or disabled). We added the body detect change as another reason to send it, without realizing the wake bug.\n* `EC_HOST_EVENT_BODY_DETECT_CHANGE`: Is the new host event dedicated purely to body detect changes (lap vs. desk mode), and is not being configured as a wake event.\n\nI\u0027m going to leave the names as they are here, unless someone has something specific in mind they believe is better.",
